# Crockpot API — /items
#
# Same shape as item-categories.http/units.http: GET is public, POST/
# PATCH/DELETE are ADMIN-only via middleware.RequireRole("ADMIN") — its
# 401/403 behavior is already covered by internal/middleware's own unit
# tests, so this file focuses on the wiring: public read, ADMIN CRUD
# happy path including allowed-units management, and the 409/404/400
# translations, run against a live server + real DB.
#
# Reuses the same one-time ADMIN bump as item-categories.http/units.http
# (see requests/README.md) — no separate setup needed if you've already
# run one of those files. Also needs one real item category and one real
# unit to reference — run item-categories.http and units.http first (or
# just note any real id from GET /item-categories / GET /units below).


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Login (ADMIN account)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Login, to get a token for the checks below.
# @name login
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_REAL_EMAIL",
  "password": "correcthorsebattery"
}

###

@authToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Fixtures — a real category and two real units to reference
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Real item category id to reference below.
# @name category
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/item-categories

###

@categoryId = {{category.response.body.$[0].id}}

### Real unit ids to reference below.
# @name units
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/units

###

@unitId1 = {{units.response.body.$[0].id}}
@unitId2 = {{units.response.body.$[1].id}}


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  GET /items (public)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — no token needed
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  POST /items (ADMIN)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 201 — creates the item this file exercises below, with two allowed units
# @name create
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-item",
  "categoryId": "{{categoryId}}",
  "allowedUnitIds": ["{{unitId1}}", "{{unitId2}}"]
}

###

@itemId = {{create.response.body.id}}

### 🚫 409 name_taken — same name as above
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-item",
  "categoryId": "{{categoryId}}"
}

###

### 🚫 400 invalid_category_id — well-formed but nonexistent category
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-item-2",
  "categoryId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}

###

### 🚫 400 invalid_unit_id — well-formed but nonexistent unit
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-item-3",
  "categoryId": "{{categoryId}}",
  "allowedUnitIds": ["00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"]
}

###

### 🚫 400 category_id_required — missing categoryId
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-item-4"
}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  PATCH /items/:id (ADMIN)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — partial update, name only (allowed units untouched)
PATCH http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-item-renamed"
}

###

### ✅ 200 — replace allowed units with just the first unit
PATCH http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "allowedUnitIds": ["{{unitId1}}"]
}

###

### ✅ 200 — clear allowed units entirely
PATCH http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "allowedUnitIds": []
}

###

### 🚫 404 not_found — a random id that doesn't exist
PATCH http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "doesn't matter"
}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  DELETE /items/:id (ADMIN)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 204 — deletes the item created above (also this file's cleanup)
DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### 🚫 404 not_found — already deleted by the request above
DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Cleanup
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Nothing dangling: the ✅ 204 delete above already removes the one
### item this file creates (and its item_allowed_units rows cascade with
### it), so a re-run from a clean server behaves the same way twice.
